# Janssens Drone Cleaning

- Stack: Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS 4, static `output: "export"`. Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using Next APIs. `LayoutProps` is generated: run `next typegen` before a bare `tsc` (`npm run typecheck` does this).
- The public brand is Janssens Drone Cleaning (JDC). Do not rename the repository or the `bdc-web` basePath/slug unless asked. The `--bdc-*` CSS prefix is an internal token.
- Never invent business facts: extra services, locations, prices, certifications, testimonials, phone, email, VAT, KBO, or permits. All of those live in `src/config/business.ts` and stay null or empty until the owner fills them in. Hide a null field. Do not render TODO text.
- Photos use the slots in `src/config/images.ts`. Until `src` is set, keep the site illustrations. No third-party stock photos.
- While `business.formEndpoint` is null, the quote form must not claim a request was sent. If `business.email` is set, a valid submit may open `mailto:` and must say the visitor still has to send it.
- Public URLs for sitemap, robots, canonical, and Open Graph come from `siteOrigin()` in `src/lib/site.ts` (`business.domain`, otherwise the GitHub Pages URL). Emit LocalBusiness JSON-LD only when `canEmitLocalBusiness()` is true. Do not add FAQPage schema.
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`: do not start GSAP timelines or other ongoing motion when it matches. Keep the skip link, labels, focus order, and WCAG AA contrast.
